#
# Example-conformance cells for the semantic-topology slice. Each cell unions the module
# with the named fixture and validates it against the canonical GENERATED projections
# (generated/shapes/{validation-shapes,constraint-shapes,procedural-constraints}.ttl) under
# the native Rust conformance harness — the slice hand-authors NO shapes.ttl; the pipeline
# DERIVES the SHACL from the module's logic:Constraint gates. gmeow:exampleFile is
# SLICE-RELATIVE; gmeow:expectedViolationCode is the COARSE native finding code
# finding_from_shacl builds as "shacl.<ConstraintComponentLocalName>". Every slice gate is a
# logic:Constraint, so every counter-example rejects with shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent;
# the SPECIFIC slice failure class is named in gmeow:conformanceRationale, and each
# counter-example isolates exactly ONE violation (AND-NO-OTHER). The conformant worked
# example lives under examples/ and is exercised as a competency cqDataFile and the example
# sweep.

@prefix gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/examples/semantic-topology/tests/> .

# === AC: every compilation records a correspondence ========================= #
ex:ecCompilationNoCorrespondence a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/compilation-no-correspondence.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "The counter-example declares a gmeow:ComplexCompilation that records its preservation/loss judgment and carries its full standpoint/world/time context but records NO gmeow:CellSourceCorrespondence, so the ∀→∃ SPARQL constraint of gmeow:CompilationMustRecordCorrespondence MUST emit shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent and NO other finding. Every other required datum is present, isolating the missing correspondence." .

# === AC: every compilation records a preservation/loss judgment ============= #
ex:ecCompilationNoLossRecord a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/compilation-no-loss-record.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "The counter-example declares a gmeow:ComplexCompilation that records its correspondence and carries its full standpoint/world/time context but records NO gmeow:CompilationPreservationRecord, so the ∀→∃ SPARQL constraint of gmeow:CompilationMustRecordLoss MUST emit shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent and NO other finding. Every other required datum is present, isolating the missing preservation/loss record." .

# === A compilation carries its standpoint/world/time context ================ #
ex:ecCompilationNoStandpointContext a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/compilation-no-standpoint-context.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "The counter-example declares a gmeow:ComplexCompilation that records its correspondence and preservation/loss judgment and carries its possible-world and time-scope context but omits its gmeow:compilationStandpoint, so the ∀→(∃∧∃∧∃) SPARQL constraint of gmeow:CompilationContextConstraint MUST emit shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent and NO other finding (gmeow:CompilationMissingContext). Every other required datum is present, isolating the missing standpoint." .

# === The governing invariant: no raw result asserted as global truth ======== #
ex:ecTopologyResultAssertedGlobalTruth a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/topology-result-asserted-as-global-truth.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "The counter-example declares a gmeow:TopologyComputation that asserts a global truth (gmeow:assertsGlobalTruth true) with no gmeow:TopologyClaim that gmeow:claimForComputation it, gmeow:extendsToGlobalSection, and gmeow:dischargesObstruction, so the ∀→∃(join) SPARQL constraint of gmeow:AssertedTopologyResultConstraint MUST emit shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent and NO other finding. gmeow:producesResult points at a gmeow:TopologyResult wrapper, so the undischarged global-truth assertion is the sole violation — a computed feature is a math:LocalSection, never automatically a global truth." .

# === A topology claim carries an attributed status ========================== #
ex:ecTopologyClaimNoAttributedStatus a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/topology-claim-no-attributed-status.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "The counter-example declares a gmeow:TopologyClaim carrying its inherited gmeow:observationMethod (satisfying the gmeow:StandpointClaim exactly-one obligation, so that is NOT the violation) and its result but carrying NO gmeow:vantage attribution, so the ∀→∃ SPARQL constraint of gmeow:TopologyClaimStatusConstraint MUST emit shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent and NO other finding (gmeow:TopologyClaimMissingStatus). The anonymous, unattributed claim is the sole violation." .

# === a computation result must not be conflated with a raw math: object ===== #
ex:ecComputationResultConflated a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/computation-result-conflated-with-math-object.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "The counter-example declares a gmeow:TopologyComputation whose gmeow:producesResult value is a raw math:PersistenceDiagram instead of a gmeow:TopologyResult wrapper, so the ∀→¬∃ SPARQL constraint of gmeow:ResultObjectConflationConstraint (matching the result's type in the math: namespace) MUST emit shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent and NO other finding (gmeow:ResultObjectConflation). The computation asserts no global truth, isolating the conflation." .

# NOTE: the conformant worked example (examples/compilation-worked.ttl) is exercised as the
# competency cqDataFile (merged, asserted lane) and by the example sweep — it is NOT
# registered as a "conforms" cell here because it references shared cross-slice grounding
# individuals (an observation method, a number system, the credence-derivation kind, the
# stability theorem, a severity, a preservation kind) that are typed only in their owning
# slices, exactly as the model-serving slice keeps its conformant demonstrators out of the
# example-conformance cells.
